---
title: Customize & Regenerate Theme
---

Now that you know how `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` is structured, it's time to edit it in your local clone and regenerate the color assets the app actually reads.

## Edit a Token

In your local clone of `vonage-video-ios-app`, open `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` and change one or more tokens under `colors` and `typography`. For example, update the primary brand color for both light and dark mode, and increase the `body-base` font size:

```json
{
  "themes": {
    "vonage": {
      "colors": {
        "light": { "primary": "#1D6FE6" },
        "dark":  { "primary": "#5FA0FF" }
      },
      "typography": {
        "desktop": {
          "body-base": { "font-size": "16px", "line-height": "22px" }
        },
        "mobile": {
          "body-base": { "font-size": "16px", "line-height": "22px" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Save the file once you've made your edit.

{% aside type="caution" %}
Stick to `colors` and the `font-size`/`line-height` values under `typography`. Changing `typography.font-family` has no effect — the app always renders text with the system's native font. Changing `borderRadius` values also has no visible effect on the built iOS app in this exercise, so there's no need to touch them.
{% /aside %}

## Regenerate `SemanticColors.xcassets`

From the `VERA/` directory of your local clone, run the theme generator script:

```sh
python3 ./Scripts/generate-app-theme.py
```

The script reads `Theme/semantics.json` and (re)generates the `VERACommonUI/VERACommonUI/Resources/SemanticColors.xcassets` asset catalog, writing one `.colorset` per semantic token with both its light and dark values. On success, you'll see:

```
✅ Generated 14 semantic colors in SemanticColors.xcassets
```

| Script | Run from | Reads | Writes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `generate-app-theme.py` | `VERA/` | `Theme/semantics.json` | `VERACommonUI/VERACommonUI/Resources/SemanticColors.xcassets` |

## Regenerate the Xcode Project

Theme tokens are compiled into the asset catalog, so the Xcode project needs to be regenerated afterward:

```sh
tuist generate
```

{% aside type="tip" %}
If Xcode still shows stale values after regenerating, run `tuist clean` first to clear Tuist's cache, then generate again:

```sh
tuist clean
tuist generate
```
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
If `semantics.json` has invalid JSON (a trailing comma, a missing quote, etc.), the generator script fails with something like:

```
❌ Error parsing JSON: Expecting ',' delimiter: line 8 column 5 (char 172)
```

Fix the JSON syntax in `VERA/Theme/semantics.json` and re-run `python3 ./Scripts/generate-app-theme.py` from `VERA/`.
{% /aside %}

Next, you'll rebuild the app in Xcode and confirm your changes.
